{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface","excerpts":[["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:master-dichotomy","Nonmembership of one half and a finite\nfatal gap","<p><em> The value <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> is\nnot in <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span> if and only if\nthere are an integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and a\nfinite set <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>\nsuch that </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nOne implication is Lemma <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#lem:fatal-gap-exclusion\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#lem:fatal-gap-exclusion\">6.37</a>. For the\nother, follow the greedy prefixes: nonmembership forces a first failure\nof the tail inequality, hence one of these gaps. The endpoint equalities\nare excluded by Lemma <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#lem:half-endpoint-kills\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#lem:half-endpoint-kills\">6.38</a>.</em></p>\n<p><em>A finite prefix and strict gap provide a nonmembership witness.\nThe tail inequality can be certified by rational truncation bounds as in\nTheorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#thm:one-sided\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:one-sided\">2.11</a>.\nMembership, in contrast, asserts that no such witness exists; failure to\nfind one in a finite search is not a proof. The reduction uses <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>, not compactness alone. The\ntotient weights fail this hypothesis, as the example after Lemma <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#lem:mersenne-tail-weight\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#lem:mersenne-tail-weight\">6.34</a>\nshows.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:perturbed-family-maximality","Perturbed-family maximality and the\nthree-branch recurrence","<p><em> Use the family and adjacent pair of\nDefinition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#defn:perturbed-family\">6.61</a>, and assume\nin addition that <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>g</mi></math></span>. At\ncapacity <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></math></span>, the largest\nadmissible updated value is <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nif <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>4</mn><mi>o</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></math></span>, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> otherwise. After this choice,\napply the take-if-possible rule to an additional weight <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>. The resulting remainder is </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\".2em\" columnalign=\"left left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>o</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>o</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>o</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>g</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>and</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>o</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>g</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>and</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\"></mo></mrow></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c1","Compactness from exact finite sums","<p><em> Suppose the cofinal exact-row condition in Definition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-d4\">6.66</a> holds. Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span>. For each <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi></math></span>, choose an exact row <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></math></span> at depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>. Proposition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-i9\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-i9\">6.98</a> gives </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mo>|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟶</mo><mn>0.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> belongs to the closed set\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span>, so its limit does too.\nNo finite support represents <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>;\nthe representing support is therefore infinite. The proof does not\nrequire the chosen rows to be nested. The unproved input is their\nexistence at unbounded depths.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c2","Infinitely many greedy skips suffice","<p><em> Suppose that the greedy remainder for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> satisfies </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∀</mi><mi>N</mi><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>:</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then exact quotient rows exist at\nunbounded depths, and <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>𝒜</mi></mrow></math></span>. A single such skip at <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>\ngives an exact row at depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>\nwithout an additional capacity hypothesis. Taking arbitrarily large\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> therefore supplies the rows\nneeded for the compactness implication in Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c1\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c1\">6.67</a>. The existence of\narbitrarily late positive skips is the hypothesis, not an established\nproperty of the greedy sequence. It is equivalent to half-membership and\nremains unproved here.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c3","A compatible family of finite\nsupports","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></math></span> whenever <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>. Define </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The four conditions\non the finite rows, required for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>, are </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"bottom top\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mtable columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.1em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></munder><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌊</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌋</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mstyle></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd><mtd><mstyle indentshift=\"2em\"><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1.</mn></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The first condition implies that the integer in\nthe next two lines is nonnegative. The second specifies the binary value\nof the upper half of the row, the third bounds that value by its\navailable number of bits, and the fourth is the exact quotient equation.\nThe maximum in the first line records natural-number subtraction at the\ncase <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>.</em></p>\n<p><em>These are the finite hypotheses of the compatible-limit\nconstruction. The bit condition fixes coordinate <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi></math></span> from row <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></math></span> onward. Unlike the independent finite\nsupports in Definition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-d4\">6.66</a>, the rows therefore\nhave a prescribed common limit. This extra structure is not, by itself,\na proof of strictness between the corresponding existence\nstatements.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c4","A sufficient quotient bound at a\ncrossing","<p><em> Consider the following condition on finite sets <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi></math></span> and integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span>: </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"0.5em 0.30000000000000004em\" data-break-align=\"middle\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>∪</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> It requires the quotient inequality at every\nstrict crossing of one half by an added weight. Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-i5\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-i5\">6.93</a> identifies this\ninequality with the binary bound needed in the finite construction. If\nthe condition holds for all such <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math></span>, the induction below produces exact\nsums at unbounded depths and hence an infinite support of value <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>. The universal crossing condition\nitself is unproved.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c5","Induction from the depth-six example","<p><em> An already-formalised induction from the endpoint-six seed\n(Definition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-i-seed\">6.97</a>) consumes\nTheorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c4\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c4\">6.70</a> at\nevery step: each protected exact row either doubles below half\n(unconditional) or recycles at its first crossing rank <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>e</mi><mo>&gt;</mo></math></span> cutoff, giving endpoint <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>e</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo></math></span> previous endpoint; protection\n(endpoint <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo></math></span>cutoff, new\nranks <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo>&gt;</mo></math></span> cutoff) is exactly what\nconverts the non-growing recycle endpoint of the bare dichotomy\n(Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-k1\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-k1\">6.127</a>)\ninto strict progress. The below-half branch never fires twice from the\nseed arithmetic, so the supply is needed at essentially every step. Its\nconclusion is the cofinal exact-row condition of Definition <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-d4\">6.66</a>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c6","The quotient condition on greedy\nprefixes","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>. The condition\non the actual greedy prefixes is </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"middle\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>c</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>G</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟹</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>c</mi><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> It asks for the quotient bound at every skipped\nrank of the specified half-greedy orbit. This restricts the crossing\ntest of Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c4\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c4\">6.70</a> to its actual\ngreedy prefixes. The finite uniqueness results justify that restriction\nwhere the cited induction uses it; they do not prove the displayed\ninequality.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c6a","Two consecutive skips","<p><em> If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></math></span> and the real half-greedy rule skips\nboth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∩</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>. Then </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The one-step\nquotient recurrence gives <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>, so Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c7\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c7\">6.75</a> supplies an exact\nrow at depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> whose new ranks\nare all greater than <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>. The\nhypothesis concerns this pair of skipped ranks; no unbounded sequence of\nsuch pairs is proved here. For the stated precritical-suffix condition\nat every skipped rank, the remaining tests are the skip-then-take cases,\nwith ranks <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>4</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>5</mn></math></span> handled separately in the cited\nproof.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c6b","A later skip after a selected block","<p><em> Suppose the real half-greedy rule skips rank <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>, takes <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and skips <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nthen the precritical suffix bound at <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span> holds. It yields sharp capacity and\nhence an exact row at depth <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>.\nThe case <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> includes Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c6a\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c6a\">6.73</a>; the proof also\npermits longer selected blocks. The arithmetic condition is precisely\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>−</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌈</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⌉</mo></math></span>.\nIts role in the proof is to make the dyadic allowance <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></span> cover the bound <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> for the earlier selected\nsupport.</em></p>\n<p><em>To obtain cofinal exact rows by this result, the stated gap\ncondition must hold at cofinally many skipped ranks <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>, not just at one rank or throughout a\nfinite sample. A finite empirical skip frequency alone gives no such\npointwise gap bound.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c7","Filling the remaining binary\npositions","<p><em> For any <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> and\nany finite <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> with\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mrow><mi>value</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and the\nsharp capacity </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> there is an exact row <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> at endpoint <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi></math></span> and every new rank strictly\nabove <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>. The implication requires\nthe displayed capacity bound, but neither a crossing condition nor a\nspecified real greedy prefix. The crossing hypothesis used in\nTheorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c4\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c4\">6.70</a> is\none way to seek that input, not an additional premise of this filling\nresult. No strict comparison between the corresponding cofinal existence\nstatements is asserted.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c8","An exact sum at depth <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>","<p><em> Under the hypotheses of\nTheorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c7\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c7\">6.75</a>,\nthere is a set <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1.</mn></math></span></div>\n<p><em> This conclusion\nforgets the additional support-extension information in that theorem. It\nis the form used when only the existence of an exact row is\nneeded.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c9","Quotients in the upper half of the\nindex range","<p><em> For integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nIndeed, the quotient is <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>, whose second\nterm is strictly between zero and one. In Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c7\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c7\">6.75</a>, the available\nranks <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> therefore\nsupply the binary weights <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. They represent every\ninteger from <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn></math></span> to <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, which explains both the\ncapacity bound and the choice of terminal depth.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c10","A finite sum from a skipped prefix","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>4</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span> satisfy </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nThen there is <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></math></span>\nand <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. No\nseparate sharp-capacity assumption is required. The binary completion in\nthe linked proof uses ranks <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>; it may therefore insert\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>. Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c7\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c7\">6.75</a> instead assumes the\nsharper <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>-bit bound so that\nevery added rank is strictly greater than <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>c</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c11","Testing one nearest dyadic boundary","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi></math></span> be nonnegative\nintegers with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>, and let\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">max</mo><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The boundary <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span> is the smallest power at\nleast <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi></math></span> among the finite list <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>; in particular <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></math></span> when <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>E</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>. The following conditions are\nequivalent: </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"middle\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>for every </mtext><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>E</mi><mtext> </mtext><mtext>or</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c12","An upper bound for the reset\nexpression","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></math></span> be an\nactual upper-reset row. Write <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math></span>\nfor its reset charge, the sum of four times the adjacent upper overshoot\nand the corresponding nonnegative correction term. The upper-reset\nidentity is </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>rem</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> The\nnonnegativity of the successor remainder therefore gives <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></span>, the side condition needed\nfor Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#record:257bm-c11\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#record:257bm-c11\">6.79</a>.\nThis argument uses the upper-reset branch assumption. It does not\nrequire the separate, conditional two-sided bound of Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.html#thm:two-sided-dyadic\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface#thm:two-sided-dyadic\">6.9</a>, and does not\nassert the charge bound at arbitrary rows.</em></p>"]],"source":"erdos257-mersenne-reasoning-surface.json?v=d132333b629d"}
